Subject: keybind-v2: the border-box rule names the key and label it sizes

What: `[data-component="keybind-v2"] *` and its `::before` / `::after` forms
become the same rule on `.ui-keybind-v2-key` and `.ui-keybind-v2-label`, the
only elements the component renders inside itself, and their pseudo-elements.
Why: a selector whose rightmost compound is `*` is tested against every element
on the page, and each test walks the element's ancestors looking for a
keybind. The session pane has none, yet these three rules were about a quarter
of its selector-matching time. Every element the rule matched before it matches
now, so no computed style changes.

diff --git a/src/v2/components/keybind-v2.css b/src/v2/components/keybind-v2.css
index 2fcd7b1e81..277e091fc7 100644
--- a/src/v2/components/keybind-v2.css
+++ b/src/v2/components/keybind-v2.css
@@ -15,9 +15,12 @@
   flex-shrink: 0;
 }
 
-[data-component="keybind-v2"] *,
-[data-component="keybind-v2"] *::before,
-[data-component="keybind-v2"] *::after {
+[data-component="keybind-v2"] .ui-keybind-v2-key,
+[data-component="keybind-v2"] .ui-keybind-v2-key::before,
+[data-component="keybind-v2"] .ui-keybind-v2-key::after,
+[data-component="keybind-v2"] .ui-keybind-v2-label,
+[data-component="keybind-v2"] .ui-keybind-v2-label::before,
+[data-component="keybind-v2"] .ui-keybind-v2-label::after {
   box-sizing: border-box;
 }
 
